# Pin line endings in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` — which the
# GitHub Windows runners ship with — rewrites every checked-out text file to
# CRLF. Vite cannot parse a CRLF `.mjs` that a `.ts` test imports, so the
# three `scripts/*.test.ts` suites died with "SyntaxError: Invalid or
# unexpected token" on Windows only, while passing on macOS and Linux. The
# defect is the checkout, not the tests, so it is fixed once here for every
# text file rather than defensively per-file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that Windows itself executes must keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.dmg binary
*.msi binary
*.deb binary
*.AppImage binary

# Copies of other projects' code, not this one's. GitHub's language bar and
# GitPulse's own language statistics both skip `linguist-vendored` paths;
# without this the ported Tauri stack under `framework/` counted as GitPulse's
# Rust. `framework` is marked here rather than added to a built-in list of
# directory names, because a project's own crate may be called that.
src-tauri/framework/** linguist-vendored
src-tauri/vendored/** linguist-vendored
